// @@@ For all indices i, if the index is greater than or equal to 0 and less than the current size of the vector, the value at the current index should be equal to the value at the next index in the previous state of the vector. If the values at the current and next indices are null, this is true.

--------------------
// @@@ The assertion states that for any index "i" that is greater than or equal to the current index and less than the size of the vector, the element at index "i" is equal to the element at index "i+1" in the previous state of the vector. If the elements at these positions are null, that is also acceptable.

--------------------
// @@@ The element at the index being removed is equal to the element that was removed next to it in the previous state of the vector.

